{
  "0": "Across all four datasets, replace absolute padded-position IDs with observed-prefix position IDs: cumsum(seq != 0), with padding ID zero. This gives the same observed prefix consistent positions during training and inference, potentially improving short-history generalization. Retain maxlen 64, the four-state 0.8/0.2 causal readout, and final-real-position inference. Preserve features, embedding tables, causal backbone, scoring, loss and optimizer; update predictor metadata consistently.",
  "1": "Across all four datasets, replace the pointwise positive/negative logistic loss with pairwise BPR: softplus(neg_score - pos_score), averaged over existing nonpadding target positions. Directly optimizing the positive-negative margin may improve candidate ranking relative to independently calibrating both scores. Keep sampled negatives, position weighting, features, embeddings, NextItNet topology, readout, optimizer and training schedule unchanged.",
  "2": "Across all four datasets, normalize log1p training-item counts by their 95th percentile among observed items, clamp to [0,1], then apply the incumbent square root. Retain zero features for unseen items and attenuation 1-0.3*feature. Robust normalization may prevent a few exceptionally frequent items from compressing the frequency feature for most histories. Use training interactions only; preserve embeddings, backbone, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer.",
  "3": "Across all four datasets, reduce tied item embedding width from 64 to 48, consistently resizing positional embeddings, prefix projection, normalization and convolution channels to match. Lower dimensional representations may regularize sparse item relationships and improve validation ranking. Retain the same six causal blocks, dilation pattern, embedding tying, initialization rule, input features, history policy, readout, dot-product scoring, loss, dropout and optimizer. Update checkpoint metadata and predictor construction consistently."
}
